DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppcciidduummpp utility displays the device address, vendor, and product name
     of PCI devices.  When no arguments are given, information on all PCI de‐
     vices in the system is shown; otherwise a single PCI domain or device may
     be specified.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd _p_c_i_d_e_v
             Specify a file to use for PCI lookups.  If specified without
             _b_u_s:_d_e_v:_f_u_n_c, all PCI devices in the domain will be shown.

     --rr _f_i_l_e
             Reads the PCI ROM from the device specified by _b_u_s:_d_e_v:_f_u_n_c, and
             writes its contents to _f_i_l_e.

     --vv      Shows detailed information about PCI devices.

     --xx      Shows a hexadecimal dump of the first 64 bytes of PCI config
             space.

     --xxxx     Shows a hexadecimal dump of the full PCI config space.

     --xxxxxx    Shows a hexadecimal dump of the PCIe extended config space.

     _b_u_s:_d_e_v:_f_u_n_c
             Show information about the PCI device specified by the tuple
             given on the command line.  If the --dd option is not given,
             _/_d_e_v_/_p_c_i is used.

FFIILLEESS
     /dev/pci*  Device files for accessing PCI domains.

